    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's an interesting take. But if we go with that hybrid model, aren't we basically ignoring the people who are at the absolute bottom of the income bracket? If we're prioritizing transit proximity and lotteries, wouldn't that be less equitable than just focusing purely on the lowest income levels first?",
