      "content": "I see where you're coming from, but some people in the council are pushing back on that. They're arguing that strict income-based allocation is actually quite inefficient and creates a \"poverty trap\" where people are punished for earning a little more. They think a more neutral, merit-based or lottery-based system is fairer to everyone in the working class, not just the most destitute. So, if you had to choose one single philosophy to base the entire mandate on, which one is actually the right one to follow?",
